course: dictionary
lesson: 137
title: Advice: a helpful idea
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Advice is an idea or opinion that someone gives you about what you should do. You can ask a parent, a teacher, a doctor or a friend for advice when you are not sure what to do. «If a friend has not paid you back, you remind them kindly and ask a parent for advice if it continues.» Here the advice is what to do next: first be kind, then ask a grown-up for help.
explain: Good advice helps you make a good choice or solve a problem. Some advice must be followed. «Children do not need diets unless a doctor says so.» So when a doctor gives advice about food or medicine, you follow it. Advice is not always right, though. «Advice on a pet-shop label isn't always the best,» so check it with a vet or an animal charity.
explain: Advice is a word with no plural, so you cannot say «an advice» or «advices». Say «a piece of advice» for one idea, or just «advice» for the general idea. Useful phrases are give advice, take someone's advice, ask for advice and follow advice.
fact: Advice means an idea or opinion about what you should do.
fact: Good advice helps you make a good choice or solve a problem.
fact: Advice is uncountable: say «a piece of advice», not «an advice».
fact: «Advice» can come from a friend, a teacher, a parent or an expert such as a doctor.
fact: Asking for advice is a smart and brave thing to do when you are stuck.
exercise: «Good advice helps you make a good choice.» What does advice mean? | A kind of food you eat at lunch | A loud shout to stop a fight | *An idea or opinion about what you should do | A rule that never changes
exercise: «If a friend has not paid you back, ask a parent for advice.» What is a smart thing to do when a problem keeps going? | Shout at your friend in front of everyone | *Ask a parent for advice | Keep it secret and hope it stops | Ignore it and wait for a year
exercise: «Advice on a pet-shop label isn't always the best.» Find and copy the word that means what a label tells you to do. | *Advice | label | always | pet
test: Which phrase is correct for one idea? | *a piece of advice | an advice | advices | an advices
test: What does «follow advice» mean? | *Do what the advice says | Give it to a friend | Ignore it every time | Write it on a wall
exam: Why is asking for advice a smart choice when you are stuck? | It means you already know everything | It means grown-ups must always do what you say | *It can help you make a good choice or solve the problem | It makes the problem bigger
